{"id": "z-cos-0000", "domain": "contracts", "category": "co_reconciliation", "title": "Change-order log reconciliation", "difficulty": "extreme", "prompt": "Reconcile the change orders on Summit Hotel Renovation. Original contract sum: $14,310,000.\n\nChange-order log (rows are in no particular order; R0, R1, R2 are revisions; negative amounts are credits):\n\n| CO | Rev | Description | Status | Amount |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| CO-06 | R0 | Additional fire dampers | Approved | $123,450 |\n| CO-04 | R1 | Unforeseen rock | Approved | $184,650 |\n| CO-01 | R0 | Added roof drains | Pending | $150,050 |\n| CO-02 | R1 | Revised storefront at grid C | Superseded | $159,400 |\n| CO-12 | R1 | Generator upsizing | Superseded | $110,850 |\n| CO-03 | R0 | Owner-requested electrical outlets | Superseded | $156,650 |\n| CO-10 | R0 | Revised stair handrails | Approved | $-154,600 |\n| CO-05 | R0 | Upgraded lobby finishes | Approved | $78,250 |\n| CO-07 | R0 | Relocated transformer pad | Rejected | $95,750 |\n| CO-02 | R2 | Revised storefront at grid C | Approved | $200,750 |\n| CO-02 | R0 | Revised storefront at grid C | Superseded | $124,000 |\n| CO-11 | R0 | Extra waterproofing at elevator pit | Pending | $43,500 |\n| CO-03 | R1 | Owner-requested electrical outlets | Pending | $134,550 |\n| CO-09 | R0 | Added data drops | Approved | $28,500 |\n| CO-13 | R0 | Added acoustic insulation | Pending | $139,250 |\n| CO-12 | R0 | Generator upsizing | Superseded | $155,600 |\n| CO-12 | R2 | Generator upsizing | Approved | $93,950 |\n| CO-04 | R0 | Unforeseen rock | Superseded | $143,200 |\n| CO-08 | R0 | Structural repair at L2 | Pending | $94,300 |\n\nOwner directive OD-01 (approved, to be priced on time and materials): value = the sum over the tickets of hours \u00d7 the labor rate + materials \u00d7 1.15 (15% markup on materials only). Labor rates per hour: Carpenter $92.00, Laborer $68.00, Electrician $118.00, Operator $105.00.\n\n| Ticket | Trade | Hours | Materials |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| T-301 | Carpenter | 6 | $2,148.20 |\n| T-302 | Operator | 2 | $2,301.66 |\n| T-303 | Electrician | 12 | $3.64 |\n| T-304 | Electrician | 4 | $713.34 |\n| T-305 | Carpenter | 10 | $1,173.79 |\n| T-306 | Electrician | 8 | $846.28 |\n| T-307 | Laborer | 8 | $2,610.62 |\n| T-308 | Electrician | 16 | $294.33 |\n| T-309 | Carpenter | 6 | $2,915.75 |\n\nBilled to date on change items in the current pay application (items not listed have billed $0):\n\n| Change item | Billed to date |\n|---|---|\n| CO-01 | $0 |\n| CO-02 | $270,350 |\n| CO-03 | $0 |\n| CO-04 | $13,500 |\n| CO-05 | $39,900 |\n| CO-06 | $62,150 |\n| CO-07 | $0 |\n| CO-09 | $31,150 |\n| CO-10 | $0 |\n| CO-11 | $0 |\n| CO-12 | $118,900 |\n| OD-01 | $18,650 |\n\nRules: only the highest revision of each CO counts and its status decides; Superseded rows never count. The revised contract sum = original + approved COs + OD-01. Pending exposure = the sum of COs whose latest status is Pending. A change item is over-billed when billed to date exceeds its approved value (an item that is not approved, or a credit, has an approved value of $0 for this test); over-billed amount = total of (billed \u2212 approved value) over those items.\n\nGive the revised contract sum, the total of approved changes (COs + OD-01), the pending exposure, the over-billed change items (as written, e.g. \"CO-04\"), and the over-billed amount.\nAnswer keys: \"revised_contract_sum\" (number), \"approved_changes_total\" (number), \"pending_exposure\" (number), \"overbilled_changes\" (array), \"overbilled_amount\" (number).", "answer": {"revised_contract_sum": 14887406.75, "approved_changes_total": 577406.75, "pending_exposure": 561650, "overbilled_changes": ["CO-02", "CO-09", "CO-12"], "overbilled_amount": 97200}, "fields": {"revised_contract_sum": {"kind": "number", "rel_tol": 0.0005, "abs_tol": 0.0}, "approved_changes_total": {"kind": "number", "rel_tol": 0.0005, "abs_tol": 0.0}, "pending_exposure": {"kind": "number", "rel_tol": 0.0005, "abs_tol": 0.0}, "overbilled_changes": {"kind": "set", "rel_tol": 0.0, "abs_tol": 0.0}, "overbilled_amount": {"kind": "number", "rel_tol": 0.001, "abs_tol": 0.0}}, "meta": {"log_rows": 19, "family": "co_reconciliation", "seed": 20261016}, "attachments": []}
{"id": "z-takeoff-0000", "domain": "estimating", "category": "addendum_takeoff", "title": "Finish takeoff through three addenda", "difficulty": "extreme", "prompt": "Floor-finish takeoff for a tenant fit-out. Room finish schedule (inside dimensions, feet-inches):\n\n| Room | Name | Size | Floor finish | Doors |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 101 | Office | 21'-8\" \u00d7 22'-3\" | VCT-1 | 1 |\n| 102 | Open office | 25'-11\" \u00d7 14'-9\" | LVT-1 | 3 |\n| 103 | Conference | 30'-9\" \u00d7 13'-2\" | VCT-1 | 2 |\n| 104 | Corridor | 26'-10\" \u00d7 19'-6\" | LVT-1 | 2 |\n| 105 | Break room | 26'-8\" \u00d7 16'-2\" | LVT-1 | 1 |\n| 106 | Toilet | 9'-4\" \u00d7 24'-8\" | LVT-1 | 2 |\n| 107 | Storage | 32'-10\" \u00d7 20'-11\" | LVT-1 | 2 |\n| 108 | Reception | 8'-5\" \u00d7 13'-5\" | LVT-1 | 1 |\n| 109 | Copy room | 27'-9\" \u00d7 15'-11\" | CPT-1 | 2 |\n| 110 | Training | 11'-4\" \u00d7 20'-9\" | PT-1 | 1 |\n| 111 | Huddle | 28'-0\" \u00d7 19'-1\" | PT-1 | 3 |\n| 112 | Mothers room | 19'-6\" \u00d7 21'-1\" | PT-1 | 2 |\n| 113 | IT closet | 18'-11\" \u00d7 22'-2\" | CPT-1 | 1 |\n| 114 | Wellness | 28'-9\" \u00d7 12'-6\" | PT-1 | 2 |\n| 115 | Lobby | 28'-5\" \u00d7 10'-3\" | PT-1 | 1 |\n\nAddendum 1: rooms 111, 108, 104, 101 change to CPT-1.\nAddendum 2: room 104 changes to VCT-1 (supersedes Addendum 1 for that room).\nAddendum 3: room 110 is not in contract (delete it entirely); rooms 112, 103 change to LVT-1.\n\nProducts:\n- CPT-1: carpet tile, sold by the box covering 48 sq ft, waste 5%, $212.40 per box\n- VCT-1: vinyl composition tile, sold by the carton covering 45 sq ft, waste 7%, $61.75 per carton\n- PT-1: porcelain tile, sold by the carton covering 15.5 sq ft, waste 10%, $58.20 per carton\n- LVT-1: luxury vinyl tile, sold by the carton covering 23.6 sq ft, waste 6%, $94.10 per carton\n- RB-1 rubber base in every room in contract: rolls of 120 lf, waste 3%, $96.00 per roll. Base length per room = room perimeter \u2212 3 ft for each door.\n\nMethod: total each product's net quantity over all rooms in contract (sq ft = length \u00d7 width), add that product's waste to the total, divide by the package coverage and round up to whole packages (a product with no area needs 0 packages). Material total = packages \u00d7 unit prices for all products and base, plus 8.875% sales tax.\n\nGive the packages of each floor product, the rolls of base, and the material total with tax.\nAnswer keys: \"packages_cpt1\" (integer), \"packages_vct1\" (integer), \"packages_pt1\" (integer), \"packages_lvt1\" (integer), \"base_rolls\" (integer), \"material_total_with_tax\" (number).", "answer": {"packages_cpt1": 44, "packages_vct1": 13, "packages_pt1": 47, "packages_lvt1": 115, "base_rolls": 10, "material_total_with_tax": 26854.29}, "fields": {"packages_cpt1": {"kind": "integer", "rel_tol": 0.0, "abs_tol": 0.0}, "packages_vct1": {"kind": "integer", "rel_tol": 0.0, "abs_tol": 0.0}, "packages_pt1": {"kind": "integer", "rel_tol": 0.0, "abs_tol": 0.0}, "packages_lvt1": {"kind": "integer", "rel_tol": 0.0, "abs_tol": 0.0}, "base_rolls": {"kind": "integer", "rel_tol": 0.0, "abs_tol": 0.0}, "material_total_with_tax": {"kind": "number", "rel_tol": 0.001, "abs_tol": 0.0}}, "meta": {"rooms": 15, "family": "addendum_takeoff", "seed": 20261016}, "attachments": []}
